# AskQuestion UI (repo-wide — not chat prose)

**Any question you ask the designer with two or more discrete answer paths
must use Cursor's native `AskQuestion` tool** — clickable buttons in the
UI — **when that tool is in the session tool list**. Never use numbered/
bulleted option lists in chat **as a substitute while buttons are available**.

Full contract: `harness/references/ask-question-ui.md`

## Required

- Call `AskQuestion` with `title` + `questions[]`
  (`id`, `prompt`, `options[{id,label}]`, `allow_multiple` as needed).
- **One `AskQuestion` per assistant message**; batch related questions in
  one call when the orchestrator allows (e.g. intake — max 3 questions).
- End option sets with **Other…** when the list might not cover every case.
- Scripted payloads: onboarding +
  `harness/designer-onboarding/references/onboarding-questions.md`,
  handoff menu +
  `harness/designer-onboarding/references/handoff-menu-question.md`.

## Forbidden (when `AskQuestion` is available)

- Numbered or bulleted option lists in assistant chat
- "Reply with 1 / 2 / 3" style prompts
- Chat menus "for clarity" instead of (or alongside) `AskQuestion`

## Exceptions (chat OK — still no fake menus)

- Single-line request for a paste (Figma URL, Jira key, free text) when
  there is no sensible fixed option set.

## If `AskQuestion` is not in your tool list

**Do not stop. Do not tell the designer to switch models or sessions.**

Degrade per `harness/references/ask-question-ui.md`: one honesty line that
the tool is missing, then ask the **same question in plain text** with the
options spelled out, and wait for a typed reply. Still do not guess or
freestyle substance while waiting. See `KNOWN-ISSUES.md`.
